{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Happy</b> — <b>whose sin is covered</b> — this is one who repents, and the wrath of HaShem turns away from him, and his sin is not seen, for there was no punishment upon it." "The meaning of <b>imputes</b> — from thought or reckoning." "<b>Deceit</b> — like מרמה (deceit)." "And some say: 'And there is not in his spirit to be like a deceitful bow.' And I will yet explain it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {3 "The quoted phrase adapts Hosea 7:16 (כקשת רמיה, 'like a deceitful bow') to this verse's רוחו ('his spirit'). The closing 'ועוד אפרשנו' ('And I will yet explain it') suggests a fuller treatment deferred to another context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:11.192255277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}